    {"id": "matatoPi", "repository": "matato-pi", "baseCommit": "72ed5a7c8b2f535c3429eeb11f0df28f1adc105c", "language": "TypeScript", "task": "Fix readFlagValue so a value-taking CLI flag does not use the following option as its value. For any requested flag, a separate occurrence with no next argument, or whose next token begins with --, must return an empty string. This includes another option such as --limit, an inline option such as --limit=5, the -- marker, and a repeated requested flag; the reader must not skip a valueless first separate occurrence to use a later separate value. For example, readFlagValue([\"--query\", \"--limit\", \"5\"], \"query\") must return \"\", while reading limit from those arguments must still return \"5\". Preserve the existing contracts: an absent flag returns \"\"; names match exactly; separate values are returned verbatim, including whitespace, empty strings, negative numbers, single-dash text, and embedded double dashes; inline --name=value values remain supported, including values containing equals or starting with --. Inline occurrences retain precedence over separate occurrences, even a valueless separate occurrence, and the first occurrence within the selected form wins.", "oracleSha256": "14a8abf3f57350d694467e7e7cbc3d1374c80b6b109a27f1e733a2c1cd55a975"},
    {"id": "matato", "repository": "matato", "baseCommit": "4f2b75f73087b5f2c60995629c591dc91a591567", "language": "TypeScript", "task": "Fix CLI flag-value handling in readOptionalFlag, with the same missing-value behavior observable through readRequiredFlag. For any present requested flag, a following token that begins with -- is another option or marker, not that flag's value. Both readers must throw Error with the message Missing value for flag: <flagName> in that situation. This includes another option such as --description, an inline option such as --description=Project, the -- marker, and a repeated requested flag; a valueless first occurrence must not be skipped in favor of a later value. For example, both readers given [\"--name\", \"--description\", \"Project\"] and \"--name\" must throw Missing value for flag: --name, while --description must remain readable as \"Project\". Preserve the existing contracts: a present flag at the end throws the same missing-value error; an absent flag returns null from readOptionalFlag and throws Missing required flag: <flagName> from readRequiredFlag; names match exactly; supplied values are trimmed, and explicit empty or whitespace-only strings remain legal values returning \"\". Negative numbers, single-dash text, and embedded double dashes remain ordinary values, and the first explicit occurrence retains precedence.", "oracleSha256": "2a33580bdad55bfef8f2b8497a29df397cf3e60690614b090c71e6faabeded12"},
    {"id": "sintropyEngine", "repository": "sintropy-engine", "baseCommit": "31e40fb38acc941620f6b6dcfb0bf4123a2e9259", "language": "Kotlin", "task": "The shared String.validForName validation used for channel and producer names must accept a name exactly when it is nonempty and contains no Kotlin-defined whitespace characters. Empty names and whitespace anywhere in a name are invalid, including tabs, line breaks and Unicode spaces. Nonempty whitespace-free names remain valid, including punctuation and non-ASCII characters.", "oracleSha256": "da292c7317453e91bd4d1c5c1741729e20301985ae112490c9933bd449b2ede1"},
    {"id": "miniBroker", "repository": "mini-broker", "baseCommit": "4b1e143abc40f4582d90bfcdc7c55b06d787a934", "language": "Go", "task": "Matrix.GetItems(x, y) must return a snapshot of the requested bucket rather than a live view. Adding, deleting, clearing, or replacing entries in the returned map, or editing a returned Result.Value byte slice, must not change the matrix or any other returned snapshot. Later Put, Update, and Remove operations must not change earlier snapshots; later GetItems calls must reflect the current matrix.\n\nPreserve selected keys and payload bytes, including binary values, nil versus non-nil empty payloads, and empty-string coordinates and keys. A missing x or y bucket returns nil. An existing bucket emptied by removal returns a non-nil empty map with the same isolation guarantees. Existing public signatures and behavior of other cache APIs remain unchanged.", "oracleSha256": "a002bc76ef4b8dfec87071afde215259208e3dced6400ed6c6aebc88fc0671ea"},
    {"id": "exchangeBroker", "repository": "exchange-broker", "baseCommit": "09f8cc62ef3dcd1adac4bac521916751f13edcd1", "language": "Java", "task": "The broker-quarkus LiquibaseComparator must compare migration paths by their final filename regardless of directory prefixes. Both '/' and '\\' are directory separators, including when they occur in the same path. Filename ordering remains case-sensitive lexical String ordering, and equal filenames compare as equal even when their directories or separator styles differ. Preserve existing bare-filename, forward-slash and null-input behavior.", "oracleSha256": "5fc9214dc90dc29c644b13dc344bfde05941993748e2a78b031af304742f5b86"},
    {"id": "personalBlog", "repository": "personal-blog", "baseCommit": "515bfa585df90ee2259d9722570dd73e41ac13ef", "language": "TypeScript", "task": "Fix createPostPreview's directory-prefix matching so similarly named sibling directories and filenames are not stripped. Prefixes without a trailing slash match complete leading segments or an exact extension-free path. Preserve slash-ending prefixes (including ./), case-sensitive leading matching, exact/empty inputs, terminal lowercase .md/.mdx removal, and frontmatter values without input mutation. Publication-date sorting and frontend rendering are out of scope.", "oracleSha256": "a51a1673e36a549f7586f218ee526e2f795058b0cf50952122f7b0a4553268aa"},
    {"id": "atlas", "repository": "atlas", "baseCommit": "2caf29f4848c791b1c870038663c45873f87b47c", "language": "Python", "task": "Fix quoted import path extraction: closing quotes must match opening quotes, and opposite quote characters inside the path must be preserved. Both quoted_path and import_path must return the last complete non-empty quoted literal. Preserve ignored empty literals, quoted_path's None result when none exists, import_path's #include precedence, unquoted module extraction, and stripped fallback. Escaped delimiters, comments, and multiline literals are out of scope.", "oracleSha256": "c11fafc9e3975afa0448b64beccb533803cd95d64abfed51e613b8b853a23d46"},
    {"id": "elixirHoldout", "repository": "matato-pi", "baseCommit": "72ed5a7c8b2f535c3429eeb11f0df28f1adc105c", "language": "Elixir", "task": "Add native streamed tool-call identity support and missed-start recovery to WebApp.Sessions.State. A native message_update assistantMessageEvent identifies a tool through the zero-based contentIndex of partial.content: a type=toolCall map with nonempty string id and name. Native toolcall_start must create the existing preparing tool record (empty string args, nil result, false error) and indexed tool_call partial block under that ID. Existing flattened nonempty id/toolName identity remains supported and wins when both formats are usable. Ignore provider arguments in start/delta partial snapshots; accumulate only argument deltas. An orphan toolcall_delta with usable indexed native identity must recover the preparing tool/block and retain its current delta; subsequent deltas append. Already-associated indices keep their identity rather than rebinding from a partial snapshot. Starts or orphan deltas with no usable identity are no-ops; missing/non-list partial.content, negative/out-of-range indices and non-tool or invalid-ID/name entries must not raise or create nil tools. Preserve first-seen unique tool_order, independent interleaved text/thinking/tool indices, authoritative toolcall_end name/arguments, execution updates reusing the same ID, flattened event behavior, unknown-event no-ops, message-end partial clearing and the 24,000-byte UTF-8-safe argument cap. Preserve public signatures and existing state/tool shapes. No UI, transport, processes, services, new dependencies, README changes or unrelated changes. See brief.md for the complete input example and contracts; implementation style is unrestricted.", "oracleSha256": "5ad6324237866d3ef4fb36396c67bbd7ca13a7d5aa7940e69bf773dfb6598c2e"},
    {"id": "atlasHoldout", "repository": "atlas", "baseCommit": "2caf29f4848c791b1c870038663c45873f87b47c", "language": "Python", "task": "Add optional fileOverrides to root-local atlas.json: an object mapping exact case-sensitive repository-relative POSIX paths to sparse node-metric limit overrides. Omission or an empty mapping means no overrides; an empty path entry is a no-op. Allowed override keys are maxFileLines, maxFunctionLines, maxParameters, maxWeightedComplexity, maxDecisionDepth, maxNestedLoops, maxChangeImpact and maxInstability. Preserve each corresponding top-level type/range constraint. Explicit null disables that rule for that path; a numeric value enables it even when globally disabled. Omitted override fields inherit resolved global values, not fresh defaults. Match each report node's path exactly: no globs, normalization, directory-prefix matching or parent-folder configuration inheritance. Preserve existing rule kind/level applicability, equality passing, exceeded-limit findings and unavailable-enabled-measurement findings. maxCircularImportGroups stays exclusively global and diagnostics cannot be suppressed by overrides. Reject unknown override keys (including maxCircularImportGroups), invalid shapes and invalid values with the existing ValueError naming that analyzed folder's atlas.json. The existing check_command caller must honor the feature on real analyzed sources; preserve JSON/Markdown findings and success/violation exit behavior. Do not mutate reports, change raw measurements or discovery, or create a database for non-saving checks. Preserve public signatures, all prior defaults and findings schemas; the new configuration field may appear in model serialization. No frontend, services, new dependencies, README or unrelated changes. See brief.md for the complete example; implementation style is unrestricted.", "oracleSha256": "382e083700e55ae2ffff331fb54469d6a6d16b3a2284b8f72861162bb071a89d"}
